# 9gate (D77, D78): 9P2000 between nodes over Noise IK, its files at its
# export (9gate(4)). It dials and announces through /net, the stack's and
# cs's, and exports from its own namespace, which holds devmgr's /dev so
# another node can mount this one's devices, and fs's tree at /fs (the
# volume, its snapshots, send and receive), which a swarm file node
# exports (D152, D153). Its handshakes run through
# factotum, granted the node's noise-ik key and nothing else (D75).
# Nothing listens until a client's ctl line says so.
service 9gate
program 9gate
use net
use cs
use devmgr
use factotum
grant factotum proto=noise-ik
mount /net net/net
mount /net cs/net after
mount /dev devmgr/dev
mount /fs fs optional
export
restart on-failure
